# Rich Media Embeds & Link Previews

This plan addresses adding rich previews (Open Graph images, site names, favicons, and YouTube embeds) to all saved links to match the premium design shown in your reference image.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> To quickly scrape metadata (like Open Graph tags) without fully loading heavy Puppeteer instances every time, I will add `cheerio` to parse the initial raw HTML of URLs. Could you confirm if adding `cheerio` as a dependency is okay?
> Also, for YouTube videos, would you prefer clicking them to play an inline embedded video or simply open the link in a new tab?

## Proposed Changes

---

### Backend Schema & Controllers

#### [MODIFY] `Backend/src/models/item.model.js`
- Add new fields to the schema:
  - `image` (String): URL of the Open Graph image/thumbnail.
  - `siteName` (String): Document's site name or domain base.
  - `favicon` (String): Shortcut icon URL.
  - `videoId` (String): Specific ID for YouTube or video platforms if applicable.

#### [MODIFY] `Backend/src/controllers/item.controller.js`
- Update the `getResurfacedItems` and `getItems` functions (or ensure they return the newly added fields to the frontend). For Qdrant mapped items, we need to pass these new fields along with title and description.

#### [MODIFY] `Backend/src/utils/qdrant.js`
- Add `image`, `siteName` and `favicon` to the payload when upserting to Qdrant, so that search/resurface functionalities can retrieve them directly from vector metadata without a database roundtrip.

---

### Backend Workers & Scraper

#### [MODIFY] `Backend/src/services/scraper.js`
- Add a fast `cheerio` payload fetch *before* running Jina/Puppeteer. This step simply parses `<meta property="og:image">`, `<meta property="og:site_name">`, and `<link rel="icon">` to get the metadata quickly.
- Detect YouTube URLs explicitly and extract the video ID (e.g., `v=...`) to store in `videoId`.

#### [MODIFY] `Backend/src/workers/itemworker.js`
- Map the parsed metadata (`image`, `siteName`, `favicon`, `videoId`) into the Mongoose document before calling `item.save()`.

---

### Frontend Components

#### [MODIFY] `Frontend/src/pages/Cluster.jsx` (and/or `Graph.jsx`)
- Upgrade the visual card representation for items inside a cluster ("folder"). 
- Render rich cards:
  - Background image or top banner mapping to `item.image`.
  - Display the `item.siteName` or `item.favicon` next to the document type.
  - For YouTube items, display a video player or high-quality thumbnail.

#### [MODIFY] `Frontend/src/pages/Search.jsx` & `Resurface.jsx`
- Replace the current plain container items with visually stunning rich cards layout as per the aesthetic requirements.
- Show the Open Graph image as a banner on top of the card or alongside the text.

